!! When to use projects

Projects structure [[Todos|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Todos]] together into cohesive outcomes. Whenever a goal requires more than one step, create a project to organize its tasks, sections, and sub-projects.

!! Creating & displaying projects

You can create projects from the [[Dashboard|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Dashboard]], by adding the <<tag Project>> tag to any tiddler, or by converting an existing task into a project from its {{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/dots}} menu.

Clicking the {{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/ui/buttons/ProjectListSettings}} button in the Projects dashboard tab lets you switch between **Card** and **List** views or reorder projects via drag & drop.

!! List vs. Kanban Board View

Inside any project tiddler, use the toolbar switcher to toggle between:

* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/checklist}} List view'' — Traditional checklist with scheduled items, sections, and expandable inline sub-tasks.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/board}} Board view'' — A drag-and-drop **Kanban board** with columns for *To Do*, *In Progress*, *Waiting*, and *Done*. Dragging a task card into a column automatically updates its status and completion state.

!! Project Sections & Modes

Click the {{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/sliders}} options button in a project's toolbar to configure:

* ''Project Mode'':
** ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/stack}} Parallel'' (default) — All unblocked open tasks are considered actionable in the [[Next Actions|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/NextActions]] tab.
** ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/checklist}} Sequential'' — Only the first unblocked open task is surfaced in Next Actions until completed.
* ''Sections'': Add named sections (e.g. *Planning*, *Implementation*, *Launch*) to group tasks within a project, and drag tasks between section headers.

!! Adding tasks & Sub-Projects

The input at the bottom of a project tiddler lets you quickly add [[Todos|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Todos]] and supports smart inline tokens (`@today`, `~tomorrow`, `!1`–`!3`, `@context`).

Project progress indicators ({{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/pie}}) and open task counts automatically roll up all nested [[Sub-Projects|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Todos]] (`SubProject`).

!! Archiving projects

The {{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/ui/buttons/ArchiveProject}} button archives a project (adding the <<tag done>> tag) so it is hidden from active lists while remaining accessible under *Show archived*.

